(6712311, 1004533, 12611, '<td valign="top">like a modern mixed-media classic.<br/> <br/>-I like where you are going with the gritty, obscured black and whites. You have a way of being able to convey a clarity of message even if the screen is dirty or dripped, or the sensor is dirty or dusty, as you noted on a previous entry. Great stuff.<br/>When I heard the title it reminded me of a song by Son Volt- "Route" the lyrics being-<br/> <br/> Standing in the neutral zone<br/> Living on sleep deprivation<br/> The rural route sleeps while the city bleeds all over itself<br/> Over the falls in a barrel is where the answers have gone<br/> And it''s now or never, too close to the latter<br/> We''re all living proof that nothing lasts<br/> And it''s here for now, transient tomorrow<br/> We''re all living proof that nothing lasts.<br/> <br/>(sorry for the long post.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-03-23 08:58:16.</i></td>', 'like a modern mixed-media classic. -I like where you are going with the gritty, obscured black and whites. You have a way of being able to convey a clarity of message even if the screen is dirty or dripped, or the sensor is dirty or dusty, as you noted on a previous entry. Great stuff.When I heard the title it reminded me of a song by Son Volt- "Route" the lyrics being-  Standing in the neutral zone Living on sleep deprivation The rural route sleeps while the city bleeds all over itself Over the falls in a barrel is where the answers have gone And it''s now or never, too close to the latter We''re all living proof that nothing lasts And it''s here for now, transient tomorrow We''re all living proof that nothing lasts. (sorry for the long post.)', '2012-03-16 09:29:42.000000', '2012-03-23 08:58:16.000000', 1),
